WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Set up once, step 1: Add the job. Top bar → Add a job

1b
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.067
Paste the job link and your interview date. See what it needs, your resume match, the gaps and a plan.

2
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.067
Set up once, step 2: Tailor your resume (Optional). Your job → Resume tab → Tailor your resume

2b
00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:13.982
Rewrite your bullets for this job’s keywords, without inventing anything.

3
00:00:13.982 --> 00:00:16.982
Set up once, step 3: Study the gaps (Optional). Resources → Study library

3b
00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:21.049
Free notes on every topic, linked from the gaps in your resume.

4
00:00:21.049 --> 00:00:24.049
Practise every day, step 1: Questions for this job. Practice → step 1, Questions for this job

4b
00:00:24.049 --> 00:00:28.040
Feedback quotes your own words. Try again and see each criterion improve.

5
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.040
Practise every day, step 2: Trade-off drill. Practice → step 2, Trade-off drill

5b
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.030
Make a design call and hold it while the interviewer pushes back.

6
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.030
Practise every day, step 3: Your stories and AI Coach. Practice → step 3, Your stories · AI Coach any time

6b
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:41.945
Write a few STAR stories. The AI Coach turns them into answers for any question, every point labelled.

7
00:00:41.945 --> 00:00:44.945
Practise every day, step 4: Mock interview. Practice → step 4, Mock interview

7b
00:00:44.945 --> 00:00:49.012
Answer out loud. Follow-ups on what you said, then content and delivery feedback.

8
00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:52.012
Interview day, step 1: Check you’re ready. Top bar → Readiness

8b
00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:56.003
One score per job and the day you’ll be ready, checked against your interview date.

9
00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:59.003
Interview day, step 2: Interview notes and debrief. Your job → Interview day → Interview notes

9b
00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:02.918
Type questions during the real interview. Afterwards they become your debrief.
